  "result": "Excellent! All 107 tests pass. Here's a summary of what I've implemented:\n\n## Customer Tier-Based Discounts\n\n**1. Added tier discount configuration** (`src/customers.js`)\n- Exported `TIER_DISCOUNTS` constant:\n  - `gold: 5` (5% discount)\n  - `silver: 2.5` (2.5% discount)  \n  - `standard: 0` (no discount)\n\n**2. Updated invoice creation** (`src/invoices.js`)\n- When a line doesn't have `discountPercent` specified (undefined), it automatically gets the customer's tier discount\n- If `discountPercent` is explicitly provided (even 0), it always takes precedence over tier discount\n- This behavior is applied only in `createInvoice`; `addLine` defaults to 0% when discountPercent is not specified\n\n**3. Comprehensive test coverage** (`test/invoices.test.js`)\n- Added 9 new tests covering:\n  - Gold tier automatic 5% discount\n  - Silver tier automatic 2.5% discount\n  - Standard tier automatic 0% discount\n  - Explicit discountPercent overriding tier (including 0 overriding tier)\n  - Multiple lines with mixed tier and explicit discounts\n  - Total calculations with tier discounts\n\n**4. Fixed render tests** (`test/render.test.js`)\n- Updated tests with specific amount expectations to use standard-tier customers (0% discount)\n- Ensures tests check the expected values without tier discount interference\n\nAll 107 tests pass (72 invoice tests + 35 other tests).",
